#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2605.22698v1 (sha256 7466fb1c1fb005e7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 660 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/brunken2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the four pre-trained models released with mlip v2
# (MACE, NequIP, ViSNet, eSEN, with partial-charge heads) trained on a
# curated SPICE2 subset of OMol25, with their hyperparameters (Appendix F)
# and MD speed on a single H100 (Table 7). Validation MAEs and RMSEs are
# shown only in Figs. 2 and 6, so there are no results. Hessian-trained
# vibrational frequencies (Table 1) and MLIPAudit scores (Table 6) are
# property benchmarks.

